-- title:
--   The four calls of one batch of the batched counting oracle write the counts of the batch
-- statement:
--   Let $x$ be an instance of the counting oracle (`Light.Filter2.OracleInst`: an Exact Triangle instance with $n$ vertices per part and weight bound $U$, a block size $s$, a modulus $p$, a place `cnt`) with precondition at free pointer $f$, the need `oNeedAt n U s p` allowed by the limits, and the tables of the oracle in memory (`BTabs`). For a batch $bt$ with $1\le kb\le$ `oKK s p` products and $bt\cdot$`oKK`$+kb\le$ `oProd n s`, the statement `oBatchTail` (two calls of writeSrc for the digit-lifted sources, preCore, and the queries), run in `oProg ++ R` in the frame of the oracle's locals, ends within `tOBTail n s p` steps; afterwards the tables are kept, the $kb\,n^2$ counts of the batch stand at `cnt + bt·oKK·n²` — the entry $e$ equals `cntOf n s p AB BC AC (bt·oKK·n² + e)`, the number of $c$ in the middle block with $p\mid w(a,b)+w(b,c)+w(a,c)$ — and every other cell below $f$ is unchanged.
